{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 23, :comments ["<b>Know well</b> [חסן — i.e., דע], <b>look to</b>, <b>sheep</b>, and <b>sufficient</b> — verses 23–27 are five joined together:" "<b>Give heed</b> — so that you not forget them, and do not set your mind on a high estate, for the treasure and the kingdom do not endure forever. It appears [that] the grasses and herbage will be gathered with you and become food for your flock, and the sheep shall be for your clothing, and the goats [in place of] a field, and the fat as your food, and the food of your household, and life by which your maidens shall live."], :book :proverbs, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 27, :notes {0 "The lemma 'חסן' in the Hebrew is puzzling; it may be a garbled or abbreviated form related to 'דע דעת' (know well) from verse 23. Translated hyper-literally without resolving."}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Proverbs -- Daat" "http://www.daat.ac.il/he-il/tanach/parshanut_hamikra/full-text/eben-ezra/mishley/"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T19:25:07.221852719Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}